in our series a more perfect union we  aim to show that what unites us as  Americans is far greater than what  divides us Arizona teachers went on  strike just over a year ago to fight for  increased funding for their schools and  better pay Carter Evans visited a second  grade class in Phoenix where one  teachers message resonated with a  complete stranger thousands of miles  away and they then decided to help what  genre is the golden flower the school  year is coming to a close at whispering  wind Academy in Phoenix but for the very  first time Elizabeth millage is not  digging into her own pocket to purchase  supplies for her second-grade class to  have dry erase markers like unbelievable  and even to have this much paper at the  end of the year it's like so excited  Arizona teachers have some of the lowest  salaries in the country just one of the  reasons they went on strike last year  mrs. millage posted her frustrations on  Facebook  sharing her salary of just over $35,000  a year a grand of which she spends on  her classroom I think it just kind of  snapped for me like I make so little  money and yet have to outfit my entire  room there's no supply closet you can go  get scotch tape no there's no paper  clips no I mean how are you supposed to  do your job without these things so I'm  at Walmart buying my own garbage can for  my classroom and I'm laughing as I'm  pushing the cart because I'm like only a  teacher what have a giant garbage can  for their classroom that they're buying  out of their own pocket her post went  viral and in New York City it caught the  eye of Ben Adam who works in real estate  he sent mrs. millage a message it just  said has anybody offered to buy your  class supplies and I thought well that's  an odd message and so I responded no and  then he reached out to me again and said  I would like to buy any supplies you  might need for the beginning of the  school year there's got to be a catch  there wasn't I felt that for very little  I can do a lot of good and I can feel  good about myself  the daily struggles have so many  educators struck a nerve with Ben of  course that  feeling is contagious and a few months  later I wanted to have the same feeling  against an acid if he needed more  supplies for the following semester and  that's what started the ball rolling  Amazon boxes started arriving in my  classroom and I'm like oh my goodness  this is crazy who is this guy  I know he's like the best then six weeks  ago Ben went one step further  he built a classroom giving website  where teachers post supplies they need  and donors from anywhere in the country  can help pay for them this is like a  wedding registry meets Secret Santa and  there is no commitment in just the past  two weeks the website is blown up 275  teachers from 31 states have requested  supplies so far 37 have had their  wishlist filled pictures and notes from  grateful teachers and kids are already  pouring in give him a box and it's like  Christmas from paints and crayons to  novels  mrs. Millett told her students they were  all gifts from their New York friend  what did you think when you found out  this guy from New York was giving you  all this stuff I think I know those rich  no no absolutely not I am NOT a wealthy  man I own a small business but I also  work he's very generous and kind and  that I would do anything to meet him and  say thank you I just want to give him a  hug I don't know if he's a hugger but I  just want to hug it no doubt it would be  a bear sized hug but for now mrs.  millage and the kids will go with a  heartfelt thank you to the guy who's in  a class of his own for CBS this morning  Carter Evans Phoenix Arizona mines me  very much a donor to ya where you can  donate to a school specifically just  exactly what he's doing too but this is  great it's wonderful proof you can help  a teacher any way anywhere and teachers  need help everywhere else you spend a  lot out of their own pockets
 

